      "reason": "The agent performed at least one confirmed browser action (clicking the Artemis link on nasa.gov, which loaded the Artemis program page). The current ChromiumRL snapshot and prior-step DOM diff clearly show the Artemis missions list, including explicit text under the heading “Artemis III” stating: “Demonstration mission in low Earth orbit, planned for 2027, to evaluate one or both commercial human landing systems developed by SpaceX and Blue Origin. The mission will launch a crew aboard Orion on the SLS (Space Launch System) rocket and will test the critical rendezvous and docking operations between Orion and the commercial lander systems needed for future lunar surface missions.” This text is in the captured visible/added content, not just task memory, so it is valid evidence. \n\nThe task asks for the next planned Artemis mission on NASA’s site and its mission name, planned launch year, destination, and primary objective. The missions list shows Artemis I (completed), Artemis II (launched in April 2026), and Artemis III with the quoted future-tense description and year 2027. From this evidence, Artemis III is correctly identified as the next planned mission. The proposed final answer’s fields match the NASA text: \n- Mission name: Artemis III (visible heading and text). \n- Planned launch year: 2027 (explicitly stated). \n- Destination: low Earth orbit (explicit in the description). \n- Primary objective: demonstration mission to evaluate commercial human landing systems and test rendezvous/docking between Orion and the landers (matches the NASA wording). \n\nThe answer does not introduce unsupported claims beyond what can reasonably be summarized from the NASA text, and it respects the constraint of using NASA as the source. The stopping condition is satisfied once these details are found. Therefore, the termination as a success is supported by the recorded browser evidence and can be accepted."
